            <ArticleTitle>Colonoscopic appendicography. A new method for the differential diagnosis of pain in the right lower quadrant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>197-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Colonoscopic appendicography is a simple diagnostic measure for surveying the position and anatomical qualities of the appendix. It is complementary to ileocolonoscopy and allows a decision to be made as to whether right lower abdominal pain is due to appendicular disease or not.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
